class.description:
A large world is split into cells, each a scene. Register them with [method add_cell], each with its area on the map, and WorldStreamer loads those within [member load_radius] of the [member observer] and drops them past [member unload_radius]. Cells load in the background and join the world a few nodes a frame within [member budget_ms], so moving never waits for them: their collision, lights and meshes arrive in slices. Beyond the detail, out to [member far_radius], a cell can show a lighter far scene instead.
Cell scenes are placed at the streamer's origin, so make them in map coordinates and keep the streamer at its world's origin (under [member WorldOrigin.world], where it moves with every shift).
[codeblock]
func _ready() -> void:
    for x in 40:
        for z in 40:
            var name := "%d_%d" % [x, z]
            $WorldStreamer.add_cell(name, Rect2(x * 250, z * 250, 250, 250), "res://world/%s.tscn" % name, "res://world/%s_far.tscn" % name)
[/codeblock]
Cells are instantiated on worker threads, several at once, so resources cell scenes share must be safe to read from several threads: imported meshes are, but a [PrimitiveMesh] isn't unless it's local to the scene. Headless, everything loads at once on the main thread, so tests run the same every time.
